    "created_at": "2023-06-21T21:30:06Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-06-21T21:32:31Z",
    "body": "Is Web IDL meant to be “language-independent” in that sense? It supports _multiple_ language bindings, but as far as I can tell, one of them must always be an ES binding. A lot of important parts of the spec (e.g. calculation of member exposure sets, types like `Promise<T>`) appear to intimately depend on the existence of an ES environment and the semantics it brings to the party, sometimes in ways that appear to have security/integrity implications.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
